      "problem": "$\\frac{2x-3y+8z}{6}=$",
      "worked_solution": "Splitting the fraction into separate terms and then simplifying the fractions in individual terms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x-3y+8z}{6} & = \\\\ \\frac{2x}{6}-\\frac{3y}{6}+\\frac{8z}{6} & = \\\\ \\frac{2}{6}\\cdot x-\\frac{3}{6}\\cdot y+\\frac{8}{6}\\cdot z & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot x-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot y+\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot z & = \\\\ \\frac{x}{3}-\\frac{y}{2}+\\frac{4z}{3} & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
